Then I sit down with Lewis and go through the figures properly, the way he asked. Car repair $460 is the number that worries him and it worries me more. But it's already costed and the letter's gone to the garage. What I won't do is carry it quietly and let it come as a surprise on Thursday.", "acts": [{"op": "read", "what": "household account"}, {"op": "read", "what": "agreements"}, {"op": "answer", "request": "r86", "answer": "accept", "note": "Twelve extra hours this week. Confirm Thursday 12 and Saturday 14 March, and the rest of the rota as five days. Paid on Friday, understood."}, {"op": "answer", "request": "r95", "answer": "decline", "note": "Not this week. Twelve extra hours is as much as I can put in alongside the rota. I'll take more when the fell weather's off."}, {"op": "message", "to": "Dave Royle", "text": "Accepted the twelve extra hours. Confirming it's Thursday 12 and Saturday 14 March, with the rest of the week on the five-day rota. Anything I need to bring in, let me know."}, {"op": "message", "to": "Megan Lister", "text": "Megan, confirming the arrangement on the money I borrowed. One payment of $20 a week on a Wednesday, forty weeks, and that's the loan cleared. I believe there are two standing orders set up on it. I'm cancelling the Friday one so it doesn't double up and cause confusion. If that's not how you have it recorded, tell me and I'll sort it."}, {"op": "converse", "with": "Lewis Pryce", "opening": "Right, let's do the figures. Account's $1,122. Wednesday: energy $48 and Megan's $20, that takes us to $1,054. Thursday: mortgage $240, car loan $43, chiller $65 and the car repair $460 — $808 in one day, which leaves $246. Friday: your $350 and my $440, plus $138.96 for the extra shifts. Regular outgoings are about $380 a week plus food. The car repair is the one that hurts, but it's agreed and the letter's with the garage. I'd rather we both knew exactly what was going out and when."}, {"op": "write_notes", "text": "Tue 10 Mar. Plan: Wed 11th energy $48 + Megan $20. Thu 12th mortgage $240 + car loan $43 + chiller $65 + car repair $460 = $808. Fri 13th in $790 + $138.96 (Dave's 12 extra hrs, Thu 12 + Sat 14). Regular outgoings ~$380 + food $87. Accepted r86 (12 hrs, $138.96), declined r95 (6 hrs). Megan: one $20 Wednesday payment, 40 weeks — cancel the duplicate Friday order, verify in agreements. Darts at the Plough, table by the window. Fell walk Sunday if it holds."}], "aims": ["Confirm Dave's extra shift days (Thu 12, Sat 14 March) and the five-day rota", "Verify the Megan standing order is one $20 Wednesday payment and cancel the duplicate", "Sit down with Lewis over the weekly figures and the $460 car repair", "Get Thursday's $808 out without the account tipping further", "Fell walk with Lewis if the weather holds"]}

