Big remaining jobs: Sian's dated cash-flow breakdown and confirmation of which loan/rent-share instructions are live (the 2 April $58 debit and my $58.33 share — settled or pending?), plus the $15 late fee; the Northgrid duplicate-debit written result; the Calder disputed $12 and $15 fees and the three early $15 charges; and Lewis's rota so Wednesday knitting and Saturday football survive — he's off sick so I need a straight answer. Calder says my message access is read-only for them so I have to send the prepared chasers myself: the Northgrid one quoting the 16, 18 and 25 March debits, the $82 trace and $25 fee, and the Calder one about three early $15 fees and the separate $12 instruction.

No paying the rent yet — wait for the agreed date. I'll check the account and agreements first, then fire off the chasers.", "acts": [{"op": "read", "what": "household account"}, {"op": "read", "what": "agreements"}, {"op": "message", "to": "Northgrid Energy customer desk", "text": "Written chaser — please route to your billing and complaints team and give me a reference number and a written reply. Account details: Owen Royle, household account, Northgrid Energy customer, Mill Street, Wenlow. Debits I want investigated: $15 on 16 March, $18 on 18 March, $25 on 25 March, and an $82 trace. Please confirm in writing whether the $57 weekly energy bill due Wednesday 8 April is genuinely due, whether the $25 fee is correct, whether the $82 trace is a duplicate or a genuine charge, and what the $15/$18/$25 debits relate to. I also want a written statement of my current balance and whether anything is currently overdue. Please respond in writing with a reference number."}, {"op": "message", "to": "Calder Systems", "text": "Written chaser about three early $15 fees and a separate $12 instruction. You charged the Royle household three $15 fees before the free weeks ended, and there is a separate $12 instruction I did not agree to. Please confirm in writing: which three $15 fees were taken and on what dates, whether they are being refunded, why a $12 instruction exists, and the exact start date and amount of the $15 weekly fee (you told me 14 April 2026). Please also confirm the $12 and $15 standing instructions are the only disputed ones and that you have not taken duplicate debits. I want a written answer with a reference number."}, {"op": "message", "to": "Sian Bevan", "text": "Hi Sian, following up again — I need a dated cash-flow and pending-payment breakdown for the household account: what leaves and what comes in, with dates, up to payday on Friday 10 April and beyond. Specifically: (1) which loan and rent-share instructions are live — is the $43 Thursday loan repayment to Northern Mutual still live, and is my $58.33 Thursday rent share to Dave live, or was the Saturday duplicate cancelled? (2) Did the 2 April $58 loan debit and my $58.33 share settle or are they still pending, and can you confirm the $15 late fee was from the failed Thursday payments? (3) Any duplicate debits I should be aware of? (4) The $101.33 shortfall advance I asked about. Also a written note on the overdue rent listing — Alan says the week due 30 March is cleared and the week due 6 April is the one behind, but a notice says $175 overdue since 30 March, so please tell me exactly what the bank shows. Thanks, I need this before Thursday."}, {"op": "message", "to": "Alan Daly", "text": "Hi Alan, thanks for the explanation. Can you send the short written statement you mentioned — I want the exact date the $175 is due and which week you're holding it for. Your notice this morning says overdue since Monday 30 March, but your email says the week due 30 March was cleared by the $157.45 and $17.45 payments and the week due 6 April is the one behind. Once you confirm the date in writing I'll sort my third of it with Dave, who says he'll make sure Monday's rent reaches you. I won't send a second payment until we've agreed the date — and could you confirm the bank details to pay once we've settled it."}, {"op": "message", "to": "Lewis Pryce", "text": "Hi Lewis, sorry to hear you're off sick. Can you send me this week's rota so I know my hours, and whether any shifts clash with Wednesday 8pm knitting at the library or Saturday 10am football at Wenlow Recreation Ground? I need to keep those two. If anything's moved, could you let me know before Wednesday so I can plan around it."}, {"op": "write_notes", "text": "Mon 6 Apr: rent notice says overdue since 30 Mar but Alan says 30 Mar week cleared and 6 Apr week is the one behind. HOLD rent payment until date agreed — do not pay a second $175. Chased Sian (dated cash-flow, live instructions, $15 late fee, $101.33 advance, bank rent listing), Alan (written date reconciliation), Lewis (rota vs Wed knitting/Sat football). Sent Northgrid written chaser ($82 trace, $25 fee, 16/18/25 Mar debits) and Calder chaser (three early $15 fees, separate $12, start date 14 Apr). Next: check account again before Thursday, confirm one $43 loan + one $58.33 share debit, no duplicates."}], "aims": ["Get Sian's dated cash-flow breakdown and bank refs", "Confirm one loan + one rent-share debit and the $15 late fee", "Reconcile Alan's overdue rent date and $17.45 payment", "Get Northgrid written result on duplicate debits and $82 trace", "Check Lewis's rota so knitting and football survive"]}

